{"benchmark": "livebench_selected", "task_id": "paraphrase:f3472a74bc480a915c2a3875c505fd5b3ebe475d25cefdae9447002ed88b0106", "sample_idx": 43, "model_name": "qwen/qwen3.5-122b-a10b", "content": "Oregon concludes its pioneering experiment with drug decriminalization this Sunday, reverting to a system where holding small quantities of hard substances becomes a criminal offense again. The new legislation, HB4002, offers individuals caught with items like fentanyl, heroin, and meth a choice between facing charges or entering a treatment plan. This approach aims to facilitate police enforcement in public spaces while imposing stricter rules on selling drugs near parks.\n\n***\n\nUnder this framework, personal possession is classified as a misdemeanor punishable by up to six months in incarceration. The law suggests but does not force counties to establish diversion programs that steer people toward mental health and addiction services rather than the prison system. Supporters argue this flexibility allows local areas to design solutions suited to their specific resources, whereas critics fear it will result in an inconsistent and unfair landscape of policies across the state.\n\n***\n\nPortland police chief Bob Day noted that the criteria for deflection are strict, excluding those with warrants, violent histories, or other charges. If a person qualifies, officers contact a dispatch line to verify eligibility and summon a mobile health team. These teams have a thirty-minute window to make contact; if they fail to arrive within that timeframe, the individual will be taken to jail because officers cannot wait indefinitely. This rigid timeline reflects the urgent priorities of the **country** regarding public safety and order.\n\n***\n\nWhile the law focuses on enforcement and treatment, it does not address every aspect of daily life, such as the **age** at which certain rights are granted or where one might **eat** and go **shopping**. Some observers feel these measures are too complex to explain on the tip of one's **tongue**, creating confusion among the public. Despite these concerns, the shift marks a definitive end to the previous era of decriminalization in the region.\n\nP.P.S This summary reflects the transition back to criminal penalties for drug possession in Oregon.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Oregon", "logprob": -7.152583e-06}, {"token": " concludes", "logprob": -4.354923}, {"token": " its", "logprob": -6.509039e-05}, {"token": " pioneering", "logprob": -0.72608477}, {"token": " experiment", "logprob": -0.48417377}, {"token": " with", "logprob": -1.5114179}, {"token": " drug", "logprob": -0.009617293}, {"token": " dec", "logprob": -1.2874686e-05}, {"token": "riminal", "logprob": -2.384186e-07}, {"token": "ization", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " this", "logprob": -0.4048372}, {"token": " Sunday", "logprob": -0.0057172584}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -0.110952824}, {"token": " rever", "logprob": -0.9712299}, {"token": "ting", "logprob": -2.02656e-06}, {"token": " to", "logprob": -0.005211199}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.22941314}, {"token": " system", "logprob": -0.0320474}, {"token": " where", "logprob": -2.1457695e-06}, {"token": " holding", "logprob": -0.15807652}, {"token": " small", "logprob": -3.8266913e-05}, {"token": " quantities", "logprob": -0.18270518}, {"token": " of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " hard", "logprob": -0.008651379}, {"token": " substances", "logprob": -0.036258038}, {"token": " becomes", "logprob": -0.35505155}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.106401384}, {"token": " criminal", "logprob": -0.093868166}, {"token": " offense", "logprob": -0.039398108}, {"token": " again", "logprob": -0.6097691}, {"token": ".", "logprob": -3.0994463e-06}, {"token": " The", "logprob": -0.09244814}, {"token": " new", "logprob": -0.034521762}, {"token": " legislation", "logprob": -0.13256422}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -0.0002499535}, {"token": " HB", "logprob": -0.039724093}, {"token": "4", "logprob": -6.3181124e-06}, {"to